WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.872
Hello.

2
00:00:01.872 --> 00:00:06.024
In this lesson we will see what a differential equation is.

3
00:00:06.024 --> 00:00:13.646
By the end you will be able to find the order of an equation and check by substitution whether a function is a solution.

4
00:00:13.896 --> 00:00:16.632
A cup of tea cools in a room.

5
00:00:16.632 --> 00:00:20.232
The hotter the tea, the faster it cools.

6
00:00:20.232 --> 00:00:24.312
The cooling rate, that is the derivative of the temperature,

7
00:00:24.312 --> 00:00:28.920
is proportional to the difference between the tea and the room temperature.

8
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.830
The unknown is not a number but the temperature as a function of time.

9
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.680
An equation linking the independent variable,

10
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.224
the unknown function and its derivatives is called an ordinary differential equation.

11
00:00:43.224 --> 00:00:47.712
The highest derivative order that appears is the order of the equation.

12
00:00:47.712 --> 00:00:50.568
Do not confuse order with degree.

13
00:00:50.568 --> 00:00:59.496
The degree is defined only when the equation can be written as a polynomial in the derivatives; then it is the power of the highest-order derivative.

14
00:00:59.496 --> 00:01:05.424
If a derivative appears, for example, under a square root or inside a sine,

15
00:01:05.424 --> 00:01:09.374
the degree is not defined in the usual sense.

16
00:01:09.624 --> 00:01:16.392
Example: the cube of the second derivative plus x times the first derivative equals sine of x.

17
00:01:16.392 --> 00:01:20.904
The highest derivative is the second one, so the order is two.

18
00:01:20.904 --> 00:01:26.784
The equation is polynomial in the derivatives, and the highest-order derivative is cubed,

19
00:01:26.784 --> 00:01:29.510
so the degree is three.

20
00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.424
Now let us check a solution.

21
00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:37.968
Is y equals C times e to the two x a solution of y prime equals two y?

22
00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:41.808
Take the derivative: two C e to the two x.

23
00:01:41.808 --> 00:01:45.048
Substitute: the difference is zero.

24
00:01:45.048 --> 00:01:49.070
So it is a solution for every value of C.

25
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.376
The graph shows solutions for several values of C.

26
00:01:53.376 --> 00:01:56.448
Each curve is called an integral curve.

27
00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:58.896
They do not cross each other.

28
00:01:58.896 --> 00:02:05.030
For C equal to zero we get y identically zero, which is also a solution.

29
00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.512
Now check yourself.

30
00:02:07.512 --> 00:02:13.478
Answer the question on the screen, then mark your answer in the question below the video.
